Cherry-pick: KiwiSDR rx_snr SNR measurement framework port (plan doc step B.4)

Imports KiwiSDR's rx/rx_snr.{h,cpp} wholesale and adapts it to Web-888:
- scheduler: TaskSleepSec/TaskWakeupF(TWF_CANCEL_DEADLINE) — Web-888 lacks
  upstream's TWF_TIME_REMAINING/NEW_DEADLINE_SEC and FROM/TO_VOID_PARAM.
- globals: freq_offset_kHz/freq_offmax_kHz plain doubles instead of
  freq.offset_kHz struct; ZOOM_CAP -> MAX_ZOOM (same value, moved from
  rx_waterfall.cpp to rx_waterfall.h).
- helpers: cfg_true()/cfg_int_() local macros (Web-888 cfg.h only has
  cfg_bool()/cfg_int()).
- dropped: ant_switch integration (snr_meas_ant_sw, antsw.snr_ant,
  ant_switch_check_set_default, snr_initial_meas_done) — Web-888's
  ant_switch extension has no SNR coupling.
- kiwi.snr_meas_active -> file-global snr_meas_active.

Replaces Web-888's hourly-only SNR block in rx/rx_util.{h,cpp} and the old
int-edge "ihr" /snr JSON. Adds: VDSL strong-signal run filter, minute-
granularity + custom intervals (snr_meas_custom_min), custom band def,
ham-band + AM BCB measurements (snr_meas_ham), imin/ant + float band edges
in /snr JSON, working "Measure SNR now" (SET snr_meas handler already
shipped in ui/admin.cpp via 0145).

Client side: admin.js gets upstream's full SNR config UI (9-entry interval
menu incl. 1/5/10 min + custom, "SNR measurement options" block, custom
band lo/hi/zoom inputs, measure-now spinner, "next measurement in N min"
countdown via id-snr-remain) minus the ant_switch checkbox; kiwi.js gets
kiwi.SNR_CUSTOM/kiwi.snr_intervals_min constants, the kiwi_snr_stats()
helper and the MSG snr_stats case (server sends snr_all/snr_hf via
MSG snr_stats after each measurement). Fork display strings kept; no
position_top_bar() call (absent in fork).

Web-888 deviations are marked with "Web-888 0149:" comments.
